       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n**Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.** That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose this high greatly raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max IR dose)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
